{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1518367-nine-days","id":1518367,"title":"Nine days...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-20T12:33:30-07:00","id":1518367,"title":"Nine days...","content":"Good evening class!<br /> I have a little thought exercise tonight for you!<br /> So... Helios got angry - ask the Bloody Man, the Followers of Set who survived the Week of the Midnight Sun or the Corax and they will confirm, the Celestine could be a grumpy one (but luckly not too bright one)!<br /> <br /> The solar storm of 2012 was a solar storm involving an unusually large and strong coronal mass ejection that occurred on July 23, 2012. It missed Earth with of approximately <i>nine days</i><br /> The region that produced the outburst was thus not pointed directly towards Earth at that time. The strength of the eruption has been predicted to be comparable - if not stronger - to the 1859 Carrington Event that caused damage to electrical equipment worldwide, which at that time consisted mostly of telegraph systems<br /> Had the CME hit the Earth, it is likely that it would have inflicted serious damage to electronic systems on a global scale. The resulting geomagnetic would have caused surges in electrical currents which would have overloaded power grids causing widespread blackouts; whole continents suddenly would have gone dark!<br /> It would have wreak havoc with power grids and satellites, criple economy, infrastrucure and navigation; - immagine the sudden loss of satelites and GPS and the loss of the powergrid<br /> Thanks to those nine days Humanity not been kicked back at lest 300-500 years if not more!<br /> <br /> But... <br /> <br /> But - and here comes the thought exercise - what if Helios have done his homework and the math and not missed Earth by <i>nine days</i>?<br /> <br /> How the Garou and the World of Darkness would have reacted in such a scenrio? <br /> <br /> How would you tell the story in your chronicles in a world where that nine days not exised to save us?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T13:02:26-07:00","id":1518370,"title":"","content":"Well, the Mokole and Corax probably get several free points of Gnosis every day at sunrise for a few days, and maybe Jam Technology gets a boost on the few hardened devices resistant to it or unconnected to the broader power grid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T13:32:20-07:00","id":1518372,"title":"","content":"So I don\u2019t think the event would plunge humanity back to the dark ages as there are enough hardened systems around and enough older tech that could be utilised.<br /> <br /> However if recent global events are anything to go by wide scale social disorder, violence and in some cases open warfare.<br /> <br /> On the face of it good news for most of the Garou nation as humanity kills off a good chunk of its population, however the benefit soon becomes apparent that it\u2019s a nightmare.<br /> <br /> There kinfolk are under attack, a percentage of humanity flees into the wilderness, the Wyrm exploits things by failsafes on polluting industries fail causing widescale environmental damage.<br /> <br /> The Weaver weakened the Wyld might seize the advantage raging across the landscape, Gorgons manifesting everywhere.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy are bound to react but their paradigm having taken a huge hit for the first time in centuries is vulnerable as the concensus\u2019s faith is technology is suddenly lost, the less technological traditions and crafts seize upon this, perhaps new reality zones arise reducing the impact of paradox.<br /> <br /> The Kindred to a degree are unaffected settled in their city fiefdoms the Princes and Bishops hunker down, having lost communication with the wider sects.<br /> However the Masquerade is threatened as cities in the dark are now prime hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> Of course if the weaver is weakened by Heleo\u2019s blow sufficiently it might lower the gauntlet even in the cities.<br /> <br /> From a campaign perspective there\u2019s lots to do at ground level there\u2019s packs defending territory, resources and kinfolk or trying to hold back environmental catastrophes as technological failsafes - fail.<br /> <br /> On an epic level this event could alter the Telluric order and challenge the pillars, science hasn\u2019t fallen but technology has - the weaver is for the first time in eons weakened, both the Wyrm and Wyld capitalise.<br /> <br /> Garou Tribes or packs dedicated to Heleos or the Wyld might take this as a sign, a sign to strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}